# A range value whose start is after its end is an error, not an empty
# range (D7): `for i in n..0` meant to count down, and `0..len(xs) - 1`
# of an empty list, would otherwise do nothing silently. The empty
# ranges are `n..n` and `n..=n-1`.
n = 3
print(0..n, 3..=2)
print(n..1)
# expect: 0..3 3..=2
# expect-error: E0522
